<h2 id="for-make-mods-simple-">for make mods simple:</h2>
<div class="boxe">

<p>for make simple <code>mods folder</code> (if you used pysch engine) you have to copie the template in :</p>
<pre><code>/mods
  <span class="hljs-built_in">base</span>-game
  template.zip    -- <span class="hljs-built_in">not</span> make yet
</code></pre><p>un-zip it and modified im, help you with the <code>readme.md</code> :].</p>

</div><h2 id="for-make-full-mods-">for make full mods:</h2>
<div class="boxe">

<p>for make full mods (modifed the source code), you have to modifie the :</p>
<pre><code>/source
  assets/
  mods/
  scripts/  -- <span class="hljs-keyword">this</span>
  ...
</code></pre><blockquote>
<p>[!WARNING]
can be hard to modifie, call me if you have any probleme.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>or</strong></p>
<p>modified the in <code>mods script folder</code>, more easy</p>
<pre><code>/myMods
  /scripts
    onGame<span class="hljs-selector-class">.js</span>
    onFreeplay<span class="hljs-selector-class">.js</span>
    ...
</code></pre><blockquote>
<p>[!NOTE]
if you want call a other script in use <code>FMS_playScript(&quot;myScript&quot;,&quot;scripts/myLittleScript.js)</code></p>
</blockquote>

</div>
<h2 id="if-you-use-the-old-version-">if you use the old version:</h2>
<div class="boxe">

<p>you have to use the source code
<del>use <a href="https://eyefly.itch.io/wapper-html-to-exe"><strong>wapper HTML to exe</strong></a></del></p>
</div>